IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lsl-employee`
IMPORT `lsl-qa`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (lsl-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with FALSE (the situation does not hold) and every
-- later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. Every situation input is a BOOLEAN, so the trap of
-- graffiti finding 31 cannot hide a read of it.
--
-- For the employee (the baseline's seat), each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked by hand from the
-- text (most taken from the baseline's own cases, lsl-cases-employee.l4), and once against the baseline export's own
-- answer on the same facts, carried into the layer's answer type. For the employer and the personal representative the
-- values are worked by hand from the text. Weeks are worked from 8 2/3 weeks for 10 years and 4 1/3 for each further 5
-- (s 8(2)), pro rata on termination after 7 years (s 8(3)).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked absence` IS AN AbsenceFacts
ASSUME `an unasked change` IS A ChangeOfEmployer
ASSUME `an unasked ending` IS A Termination
ASSUME `an unasked pay` IS A PayFacts
ASSUME `an unasked mode` IS A LeaveMode

`as the employee` MEANS `I am an employee in Western Australia`
`as the employer` MEANS `I employ people in Western Australia`
`as the personal representative` MEANS `I am the personal representative of an employee who has died`

-- The absences, changes of employer and pay of the baseline's cases (lsl-cases-employee.l4), restated here: a case
-- file is not imported.
`paid annual leave` MEANS AbsenceFacts WITH
    `the absence` IS `leave of a kind listed in s 6(1)`
    `it was paid` IS TRUE
    `I am a casual or seasonal employee` IS FALSE
    `I came back as soon as practicable` IS FALSE
    `I returned on the terms that settled the dispute` IS FALSE
    `my employer gave written notice within 14 days that continuity was broken` IS FALSE
    `months until my employer re-employed me` IS 0
    `the dismissal was for slackness of trade` IS FALSE
    `if the dismissal was made to avoid long service leave or annual leave` IS FALSE

`unpaid parental leave` MEANS AbsenceFacts WITH
    `the absence` IS `leave of a kind listed in s 6(1)`
